---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="DMARC Monitoring - See Who Sends Email as Your Domain"
  description="DMARC monitoring, in development: aggregate reports from Gmail, Microsoft and Yahoo parsed into a table of every service sending as your domain, with a path to p=reject. Join early access."
>
  <div class="mx-auto max-w-4xl px-4 py-16">
    <div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-3">
      <p class="font-mono text-xs uppercase tracking-[0.2em] text-accent">Product</p>
      <span class="rounded-full border border-warn/40 bg-warn/10 px-3 py-0.5 font-mono text-[10px] uppercase tracking-wider text-warn">In development - join early access</span>
    </div>
    <h1 class="font-display mt-3 text-4xl font-bold tracking-tight text-ink sm:text-5xl">
      Know every service that sends email as your domain.
    </h1>

    <div class="pd-answer" data-vs="answer">
      <p class="text-lg leading-relaxed text-ink-dim">DMARC monitoring is the continuous collection and analysis of the aggregate reports mailbox providers already send, turning raw XML into a live list of every source sending mail as your domain with its authentication results.</p>
    </div>    <p class="mt-4 max-w-2xl text-lg text-ink-dim">
      Gmail, Microsoft, and Yahoo already email you daily DMARC reports listing every server that
      used your domain - useful data nobody reads because it arrives as zipped XML. DMARC
      monitoring reads it for you.
    </p>

    <div class="mt-8 flex flex-wrap gap-4">
      <a href="/early-access/" class="btn-cta btn-shimmer px-5 py-2.5 text-sm">Join early access</a>
      <a href="/dmarc-report-analyzer/" class="border border-line bg-panel-2 px-5 py-2.5 text-sm font-semibold text-ink hover:border-accent/40">Try the free report analyzer today</a>
    </div>

    <div class="mt-14 grid gap-5 md:grid-cols-3">
      {[
        {
          step: '1',
          title: 'Add one DNS record',
          desc: 'Add our reporting address to your DMARC record (rua=). Nothing else changes - your mail flow is untouched, and your own DNS stays where it is.',
        },
        {
          step: '2',
          title: 'Reports flow in daily',
          desc: 'Mailbox providers send aggregate reports to that address automatically. We unzip and parse each one: source IPs, volumes, SPF/DKIM results, alignment.',
        },
        {
          step: '3',
          title: 'See who is sending as you',
          desc: 'A plain table: every sending service identified by name - Google Workspace, SendGrid, your newsletter tool - with pass/fail and "this is me / not me" for each.',
        },
      ].map((s) => (
        <div class="rounded-xl border border-line bg-panel/60 p-5">
          <p class="font-mono text-xs text-accent">STEP {s.step}</p>
          <h2 class="font-display mt-2 font-semibold text-ink">{s.title}</h2>
          <p class="mt-2 text-sm leading-relaxed text-ink-dim">{s.desc}</p>
        </div>
      ))}
    </div>

    <div class="rich-text mt-14">
      <h2>What it answers</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>Which services send mail as your domain today - including ones you forgot or an attacker added.</li>
        <li>Why legitimate mail fails SPF or DKIM (misaligned return-path, missing include, wrong selector).</li>
        <li>When it is safe to move your policy from <code>p=none</code> to <code>p=quarantine</code> to <code>p=reject</code> - with a checklist instead of a guess.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Free today, before launch</h2>
      <ul>
        <li><a href="/dmarc-record-checker/" class="text-accent">DMARC Record Checker</a> - validate your current record and policy.</li>
        <li><a href="/dmarc-report-analyzer/" class="text-accent">DMARC Report Analyzer</a> - upload a report file you already received and see it parsed.</li>
        <li><a href="/dmarc-record-generator/" class="text-accent">DMARC Record Generator</a> - build the record, including the reporting address.</li>
        <li><a href="/dmarc/" class="text-accent">The DMARC guide</a> - how policies, alignment, and reports actually work.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Early access</h2>
      <p>
        Monitoring is being built now. Early-access members get the first accounts, the launch
        free tier, and a direct line on features - <a href="/early-access/" class="text-accent">request access</a>.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
